window.L1MS={"app_name":"DNS Test","a_logo":"1ms.dog","a_theme":"Theme","a_close":"Close","a_prev":"Previous","a_next":"Next","th_system":"Theme: system","th_light":"Theme: light","th_dark":"Theme: dark","rerun":"Test again","best_k":"Fastest for you","w_real":"measured","w_est":"estimated","lead_k":"Fastest so far","lead_sub":"{n} of {of} have answered · leading for now","lead_sub_one":"{n} of {of} has answered · leading for now","c_dns":"DNS","c_doh":"DoH","c_udp":"UDP ≈","c_dot":"DoT ≈","c_unc":"First lookup","tip_est":"An estimate. Browsers can't send UDP or DoT queries, so this times an encrypted query (DoH) to the same server instead: same distance, same server doing the work, so it takes about as long.","tip_unc":"A name nobody has looked up yet: the resolver first has to ask the site's own DNS servers, so it's slower. How much slower depends on where those servers are, so it isn't ranked.","tip_sec":"Checks DNSSEC (domain signatures): answers with a bad signature are refused, so they can't be forged.","tip_loss":"{p}% of queries got no answer","tip_noest":"This resolver's plain DNS server doesn't speak HTTPS, so a browser can't time it","tip_none":"Not offered","tip_rewrite":"When a name doesn't exist, it answers with an address (usually an ad page) instead of saying so","rewrites":"redirects","e_timeout":"timeout","e_fail":"no answer","progress":"{n} / {of}","done":"Done in {s} s · popular names used: {names}","none_up":"No resolver answered","win_sub":"Fastest of {n}, {d} ms ahead of {second}","use_h":"How to use it","use_udp":"DNS servers","use_dot":"Private DNS (DoT)","use_doh":"DNS over HTTPS","alt_udp":"If you can only enter a plain DNS address (on most routers, say), the fastest is {name}: about {ms} ms ({ips}).","cn_note":"In mainland China, plain DNS queries to resolvers abroad get forged answers for blocked sites. So for those resolvers the UDP estimate shows speed only, not whether they'll work.","cli_h":"Measure UDP, DoT and DoQ for real on a server","cli_sub":"A browser can only estimate UDP and DoT. Run this command on a VPS, a Linux machine or a router to measure all five protocols, compared with the DNS that machine uses now.","cli_btn":"Command line","cli_more":"More options","cli_install":"Install and run (Linux, macOS, routers)","cli_install_s":"Installs dnstest to /usr/local/bin (or ~/.local/bin) and opens a menu where you pick what to test. Type dnstest any time to test again.","cli_once":"Run once without installing","cli_wget":"No curl? Use wget","cli_opts":"Useful options","cli_o_proto":"Only some protocols","cli_o_res":"Only some resolvers (dnstest --list shows them all)","cli_o_v6":"Use IPv6","cli_o_json":"Output JSON","cli_win":"Windows","cli_win_s":"Run in PowerShell to install dnstest and open its menu. Or download the program directly:","cli_src":"Source code and all releases","share":"Share","share_text":"My fastest DNS is {name} at {ms} ms. What's yours?","share_title":"My fastest DNS: {name}, {ms} ms · DNS Test","emb_head":"Your fastest DNS: {name}, {ms} ms","emb_down":"{n} resolvers can't be reached from your network","emb_down_one":"{n} resolver can't be reached from your network","emb_nodnssec":"{name} doesn't check DNSSEC (domain signatures)","emb_rewrite":"{name} sends names that don't exist to another address (usually an ad page)","emb_fail":"No resolver answered: an ad blocker or firewall may be blocking encrypted DNS (DoH) requests","share_desc":"{n} public DNS resolvers timed from one network: {name} {ms} ms, then {second} {ms2} ms. See which is fastest on yours.","share_desc1":"{n} public DNS resolvers timed from one network: {name} {ms} ms. See which is fastest on yours.","card_head":"My fastest DNS","card_sub":"{n} public resolvers timed · DoH measured, UDP and DoT estimated","card_sub_one":"{n} public resolver timed · DoH measured, UDP and DoT estimated","share_text_self":"{name} answers in {ms} ms on my network. How about yours?","share_title_self":"{name} on my network: {ms} ms · DNS Test","share_desc_self":"{name} timed from one network: DoH {ms} ms. See how fast it is on yours.","card_head_self":"Timed on my network","card_sub_self":"DoH measured, UDP and DoT estimated","who_link":"Which DNS is your device really using? Check for DNS leaks on Who Are You","c_doq":"DoQ ≈","tip_est_doq":"An estimate. Browsers can't send DNS over QUIC either. A resolver's DoQ is the same server as its DoT, one round trip per query on an open connection, so this is the DoT estimate. The command-line tool measures DoQ for real.","sp_title":"Are public DNS resolvers up? Status from Tokyo · DNS Test","sp_desc":"Every resolver DNS Test lists, probed from Tokyo every 10 minutes over UDP, IPv6, DoT, DoH and DoQ: each protocol now, the last 24 hours, uptime over a day, a week and a month, and every outage.","sp_h1":"Are these resolvers up?","sp_intro":"1ms.dog's server in Tokyo asks every resolver for example.com every 10 minutes, over each protocol it offers. A protocol counts as down when no answer comes within 4 seconds. This is Tokyo's view: if a resolver is up here but doesn't answer you, your network is probably blocking it.","sp_wait":"Loading…","sp_meta":"Tokyo, every 10 minutes · last run {t}","sp_stale":"Last run {t}: the Tokyo watch may have stopped","sp_err":"Couldn't load the results from Tokyo. Try again later.","sp_off":"This copy of the page doesn't load the 1ms.dog status.","sp_sum":"All protocols up: {ok} / {n}","sp_ok":"up","sp_part":"partly down","sp_bad":"down","sp_cell":"one cell per hour","sp_c_24":"Last 24 hours","sp_c_up24":"24 h","sp_c_up7":"7 days","sp_c_up30":"30 days","sp_out_h":"Outages in the last 24 hours","sp_none":"None: every probe got an answer.","sp_now":"now","sp_link":"Are these resolvers up? Status from Tokyo","mine_h":"The DNS your device really uses","mine_wait":"Looking…","mine_fail":"Couldn't tell: your network may be blocking port 2053 of l.1ms.dog.","mine_ecs_yes":"It tells websites' DNS servers your network ({net}), so CDNs can pick a server near you.","mine_ecs_no":"It doesn't tell websites' DNS servers your network, so CDNs pick a server near the resolver, not near you.","mine_ecs_late":"Its first query didn't carry your network; later ones did ({net}).","mine_far":"It is in {where} and your connection comes out in {here}: websites may send you to a server far away.","mine_credit":"IP locations: {db}","node_h":"Serving you from","f_node":"{name} serves you from","node_ecs":"passes on your network","node_noecs":"doesn't pass on your network","node_none":"not seen","tk_h":"Uptime (Tokyo)","tk_v":"7 days {d7} · 30 days {d30}","tk_up":"It answers from Tokyo ({ms} ms), so your network is most likely blocking it.","tk_down":"It doesn't answer from Tokyo either, so it is probably down.","speed_link":"DNS looks fine but things are still slow? Test your speed","check_link":"Run a full checkup","asn_tip":"Look up {as} in ASN Lookup","copied":"Copied","rules_btn":"Direct rules","rules_h":"Direct rules: test your own network, not your proxy","rules_sub":"With a proxy on, your browser reaches the resolvers through it, so the test times the proxy's route. These rules send only the addresses this test uses DIRECT. All other traffic stays as it is.","rules_remote_h":"Recommended: remote rule set","rules_remote_s":"Your proxy app fetches the rules from this site and keeps them up to date when resolvers change. You only add it once.","rules_inline_h":"Or paste all the rules ({n}, with comments)","rules_inline_only":"This app doesn't support remote rule sets, so paste the rules ({n}, with comments)","rules_top":"put it above your other rules","rules_fakeip":"in fake-ip mode, these hosts must resolve to their real addresses","rules_plain":"Plain list","rules_after":"Then reload your proxy's config and test again.","copy":"Copy","v_join":", ","d_dot":"DoT / Private DNS","d_blocks":"Blocks","blocks_ads":"ads and trackers","blocks_malware":"malware and phishing sites","blocks_phishing":"phishing sites","d_site":"Website","f_run":"Testing","f_done":"Your result","f_wait":"Waiting for it to answer…","f_down":"Can't be reached from your network","f_sub":"First lookup (a name not cached yet): {unc} ms","f_all":"Test all {n} resolvers to see which is fastest"};
